1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,940
I'm going to crush his spirit, his will to fight, to stand, and to resist.

2
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:18,580
I'll make him see, I'll prove to him that all his hard work and confidence mean absolutely nothing.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,180
You can't attack me anyway.

4
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:49,060
Not only a human in my corner so that he is born.

5
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:56,000
If you get started or not, the dream will remember her score ever.

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,500
You can smile again

7
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,700
太陽浴びて

8
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,500
You can fly away

9
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:10,500
世界は君の輝きを待ってる

10
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,500
大地を踏みしめて

11
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:16,500
君は目覚めてゆく

12
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,500
天使の微笑みで

13
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:22,500
連れ出して

14
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,000
始まりはいつでも

15
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,500
細くないさ

16
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,500
何度でも立ち上がれ

17
00:01:52,500 --> 00:02:04,500
期待して

18
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,200
独卟 Hawk

19
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,000
地域の敵に

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
一番に

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,500
近くvoll転ばせました

22
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:21,000
でも進む Ganon

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,440
Hmm, Gyo, huh?

24
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:29,160
The moment I grasped his arm, he focused his aura there to block my attack.

25
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,680
You fool! You think you've figured me out now, don't you?

26
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:48,920
Oh, what's the matter? That was just a simple body blow.

27
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:54,360
If you focus your aura wherever I grab you, then you leave yourself open everywhere else.

28
00:02:55,540 --> 00:03:00,580
Pointless. In fact, it was worse than pointless. It even backfired on you.

29
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,060
It's just like Bisky said.

30
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:11,820
You won't be smiling much longer.

31
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:19,760
One more, and you're finished.

32
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:31,040
Impossible. That was the hardest hit so far. He shouldn't have been able to counter.

33
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:34,800
But he did, and that means that he kept the damage to a minimum.

34
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:40,200
In other words, he blocked me with standard defenses, not by relying on aura.

35
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,980
Did he just guess that I wouldn't set off an explosion?

36
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:47,200
No. That look!

37
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:53,600
So hey, Bisky, how come Genthrou doesn't get burned by his own explosions?

38
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,020
Oh, it's pretty simple, actually.

39
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:01,620
You see, he covers his hand with more aura than he uses to detonate.

40
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:03,340
Oh, I get it.

41
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:07,200
It's a technique that requires quite a large reserve of aura.

42
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,020
Now's as good a time as any.

43
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,020
Let's see if you can tell, huh?

44
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,120
Excellent reaction.

45
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,520
You've almost perfected Gyo.

46
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:20,500
All right, now one more time.

47
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,400
Huh?

48
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,140
You could tell the difference?

49
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,860
Yeah. You used less aura the second time, didn't you?

50
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,000
Yes, that's right. You pass.

51
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:34,960
Now that you can tell the difference, you're going to have a much easier time facing him.

52
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:40,000
Right before Genthrou uses his little flower, he'll use Gyo on his hand.

53
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:46,520
But when he's pretending to use his ability, he's going to attack you somewhere else and won't bother using Gyo.

54
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:47,380
Huh.

55
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:56,220
If you can feel whether the hand touching you is protected by Gyo or not, that means you'll be able to thwart his attacks and feints to some extent.

56
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:02,740
I see. You knew from my Gyo. Very clever.

57
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:11,580
Like I said before, the shallow strategy you're using, it's going to backfire.

58
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:21,680
If my little flower catches you when you're not using enough aura to defend yourself, a hit to the face will blow your eyes, your nose, and your mouth clean away.

59
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:30,520
A hit to the arms or legs will incinerate your skin, severely damaging any nerves or muscle. You'll have no fingers or toes left.

60
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:37,360
It's impossible for you to guard against all of my Gyo attacks with your Gyo.

61
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:44,200
So now what? I've no interest in continuing this. This fight has shown me something.

62
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:55,040
You have talent as well as a promising future, filled with opportunities. Don't you think that throwing it all away just for the sake of pride is meaningless?

63
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:58,040
Come on, brat. Give up already.

64
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:07,880
If he shows signs that he's going to use both hands to blow you up, that's a red flag. And you must focus on following the plan exactly.

65
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:20,580
Biscuit, Killua, I'm sorry. I know it's selfish of me, but I've got to go with my gut. I have to try. Because... I just had a great idea.

66
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:27,640
Well, if you really feel that way, then just give up, Ganthru!

67
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:31,880
How unfortunate.

68
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:41,880
Let me show you that there are some fates even worse than dying. I'll give you an example.

69
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:52,880
First, I'll blow up both of your arms. Use Gyo to protect the one you want to keep. And after that's done, I'll blow up your remaining arm along with your left leg.

70
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:59,880
Again, use Gyo to protect the one you want to keep. We'll continue in that fashion until you're out of limbs.

71
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:02,880
Yeah, we'll just go ahead and try.

72
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:03,880
All right.

73
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:08,880
Take this!

74
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,880
What... what just happened?

75
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:30,880
Blood... I'm injured? Was I attacked?

76
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,880
Show me Rock!

77
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:35,880
Crap!

78
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:38,880
Move! Get out of the way!

79
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,880
John... Ken...

80
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:44,880
Rock!

81
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:55,880
Did he hit me? No. I just tripped.

82
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:59,880
What the hell was that? What happened?

83
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:09,880
Wait. Now I get it. This little brat sacrificed both hands!

84
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:25,880
But it seems the damage wasn't distributed evenly. He probably gave up on his left hand. He protected his right with 30% of his aura, and focused the remaining 70% in his legs to attack me!

85
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:46,880
I use Aura to blow up targets as well as to shield my hand from the blast. But if I attack with both hands, it leaves the rest of my body defenseless. He took advantage of that. Still, no sane person would ever actually try it!

86
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:51,880
At least, I gave him a pretty good scare.

87
00:08:55,880 --> 00:09:01,880
This hurts so bad, I feel like I'm gonna die! But... I'm going for it!

88
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,880
That's... enough.

89
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,880
Wait. Is he giving up?

90
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:20,880
Of course. It all makes sense. He's lost his left hand, and his right is badly injured. He did manage to land a hit on me. Perhaps that satisfied him.

91
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:29,880
Okay, I'm done being selfish now. Time to get serious! Come on, and fight me!

92
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:34,880
What is wrong with this brat? He's completely insane!

93
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:48,880
Book!

94
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:54,880
A card? He shouldn't have anything I need to worry about.

95
00:09:56,880 --> 00:10:01,880
Wait, it transformed? Paladin's necklace? What is he planning?

96
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:09,880
This is your last chance to surrender. Once I use this, you could die. So think about it carefully.

97
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:17,880
It's obvious that you're bluffing. But wait. This is my chance. Book.

98
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:22,880
I give up. You're never going to admit defeat. That much is clear.

99
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,880
Take what you want.

100
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:34,880
I'll silence him. Crushing his windpipe and knocking him out would be best. Then I can take the cards from his binder.

101
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:38,880
But I do have one request. What?

102
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,880
I only ask that you leave me this card right here.

103
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:50,880
He blocked my second attack with Gyo!

104
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:57,880
But at least I managed to crush his throat, which means he won't be able to save Book or Gain anymore!

105
00:10:57,880 --> 00:11:04,880
Gain through! That's the worst decision you could have possibly made!

106
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:08,880
One minute!

107
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:14,880
That smell!

108
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:22,880
He can't use this little flower anymore! I'm gonna take him down!

109
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,880
Book!

110
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,880
Oh, I see. This is gasoline. That's a good one.

111
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:32,880
It's true that I can't use little flower now. However, I have another ability. Countdown.

112
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:45,880
You may recall that I can set a bomb on someone, and all I have to do is touch them and say the word bomber.

113
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:53,880
And if you intend to disarm it, then your only recourse would be to touch me while saying I caught the bomber.

114
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:59,880
This one is ten times stronger than little flower, so you won't be able to block it with Nen.

115
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:08,880
All of the activation requirements have been met. If I touch you and say bomber, the countdown will begin.

116
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:13,880
I'd run if I were you. Well, if you still have the strength.

117
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:17,880
Oh, yeah. My requirements have been met, too!

118
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:20,880
Now show me, Rock!

119
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:28,880
His earlier attack... I can't get too close. Is he keeping me back?

120
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:34,880
John... Gen... Rock!

121
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:46,880
A pit trap! But why? He's falling, too!

122
00:12:50,880 --> 00:13:06,880
It's deep. Far too deep to climb out. Still, he's in the same position. Doesn't he see that he's cornered himself?

123
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:11,880
He's gone!

124
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:13,880
Genthru...

125
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,880
Genthru...

126
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:23,880
If a card is removed from the binder for a minute, it reverts to an item!

127
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:31,880
A rock!

128
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:44,880
G scheduled for 1998, it isn't a insane neutraláb tanto at once.

129
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:46,880
I don't know why, huh?

130
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:52,880
Is it in an animal park?

131
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:53,880
Show me... Rock.

132
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,880
Jan... Get...

133
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,880
No, wait! Hold on, I surrender! I surrender!

134
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:05,880
Rock!

135
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:31,680
You're awake?

136
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:34,000
Hurry and get your binder out.

137
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:35,480
That's right.

138
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:39,780
We want you to return all the cards you stole from the people you betrayed.

139
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:42,740
On one condition.

140
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:48,020
Use Angel's breath to heal Bara of his injuries.

141
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,880
We have a clone card.

142
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,800
Don't worry about it.

143
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,140
That was always a part of the plan.

144
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:59,600
We already prepared six copies of clone for just such an occasion.

145
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:04,780
Book.

146
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:09,700
Game!

147
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:22,860
What manner of aid do you wish of me?

148
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:25,060
We need you to heal his throat.

149
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,480
And while you're at it, both of his hands, too.

150
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:28,800
Scratch that.

151
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,560
Just fix everything wrong with him.

152
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,760
That is a simple task.

153
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:36,700
And so I shall restore his body to its former state.

154
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,160
Yes!

155
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,220
I'm healed!

156
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:54,260
Now, fare thee well.

157
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:57,580
Right.

158
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:58,720
Here it is.

159
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:00,700
The extra Angel's breath card.

160
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:04,620
Gain!

161
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:13,680
Next up is Killua.

162
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,500
Okay, Gunthru.

163
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,500
We're going to use your binder now.

164
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,500
Do as you please.

165
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:21,560
And clone on.

166
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,360
Attention.

167
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:26,620
Angel's breath has reached its maximum card limit.

168
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:28,220
The clone will be destroyed.

169
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:31,860
Hey, wait a minute!

170
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:33,220
What just happened?

171
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:34,780
Did I mess it all up?

172
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:35,740
No.

173
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:36,860
It's Gorenu.

174
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:42,400
He used either clone or transform to increase the number of Angel's breath vouchers.

175
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:45,220
Two of his vouchers became Angel's breath.

176
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:46,720
That must be why.

177
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,160
Attention.

178
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:53,360
Another player has used contact to reach you.

179
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:55,820
Hey, it's Gorenu.

180
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,640
Looks like you did it, huh?

181
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:01,640
But I don't approve.

182
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:07,360
If you use Angel's breath to heal these murderers, then the trade is off.

183
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:08,900
Could I use it?

184
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:10,000
Yeah, of course.

185
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:12,040
But I'm an assassin.

186
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:12,960
Huh?

187
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:14,660
Sure they've killed.

188
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:15,820
I've killed more.

189
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:20,660
Every player in this game risks their life in one way or another.

190
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:23,380
That doesn't mean it's okay to kill people.

191
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:28,640
But all the people I killed weren't nearly as ready to die as the ones these guys did.

192
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:31,460
I'm way worse than they could ever be.

193
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:32,820
You're wrong.

194
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:34,340
You're not at all like them.

195
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:36,760
I mean, I like you, but these guys?

196
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,160
I hate their guts.

197
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,180
Yeah, that isn't very logical.

198
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:41,980
Oh, forget logic.

199
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:43,320
It's how I feel.

200
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:45,340
Don't you feel the same way?

201
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:47,800
But it's not our place to judge.

202
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:51,040
We don't think it's right to let them die just because we hate them.

203
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:54,520
Both sides risk their lives in battle.

204
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:57,120
And both are prepared to kill if necessary.

205
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:01,500
But when the fight's over, well, those rules cease to apply.

206
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:05,480
I still haven't forgiven Genthru for killing all those other players.

207
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:06,880
Not yet, at least.

208
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:10,320
But before the fight even started, the three of us agreed.

209
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:13,540
We'd bring six clone cards with us just in case.

210
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:18,360
I don't really remember why we decided that, but I do know one thing.

211
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:20,900
It wasn't based on logic or reason.

212
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,700
It just made sense to all of us.

213
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:30,180
Once the fight was over and we'd obtain the Angel's Breath card, we would use it on whoever was hurt.

214
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:34,720
We made the decision together, so we wanted to stick to it.

215
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:36,940
But I get how you feel, Mr. Gerenu.

216
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,440
I guess it can't be helped.

217
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,900
Sorry, Killua.

218
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:42,640
Could you wait a little longer?

219
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:44,580
Not a problem.

220
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:47,320
My hands will eventually heal on their own.

221
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:54,180
Things have changed, so we can't use clone anymore.

222
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,820
And there's just one Angel's Breath left.

223
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:57,800
Hang on.

224
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:58,640
Only one?

225
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,760
Are you talking about the original card?

226
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:03,640
I want you to use it on Genthru.

227
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,120
I'm gonna be alright.

228
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:16,820
Let's use a company to go to Masadora.

229
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:17,700
Yeah.

230
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:19,560
Hey, wait up!

231
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:21,900
Alright, you can have Angel's Breath.

232
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,340
Whatever you guys want.

233
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:24,760
Really?

234
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:25,720
You're sure?

235
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:31,020
Well, to be honest, even before you told me everything, I decided to give it to you.

236
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:34,840
And not just Angel's Breath, but all the cards that we gathered in the game.

237
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,840
We all agreed.

238
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,980
Tezgera, his team, and me.

239
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:42,780
Thing is, we all decided to quit the game.

240
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,580
Oh, wow.

241
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:48,940
I'm all better.

242
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:52,100
So, Mr. Batera...

243
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:52,520
Yeah.

244
00:19:52,980 --> 00:19:55,520
He paid off Team Tezgera for breaking the contract.

245
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,920
I settled for four billion Jenny.

246
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:58,940
Wait, four billion?

247
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,660
You want to put something on over?

